From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMANET Firmware <noreply@openmanet.local>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] batman-adv: bound BATMAN_IV flooding for HaLow

The upstream TTL of 50 is excessive for the low-rate, shared HaLow medium.
Limit new OGM, broadcast, and unicast packets to eight mesh hops. BATMAN_IV's
runtime hop penalty remains 30, matching the ESP32 factor of 225/255.
---
 .../patches/999-edgez-halow-ttl.patch          | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/feeds/routing/batman-adv/patches/999-edgez-halow-ttl.patch b/feeds/routing/batman-adv/patches/999-edgez-halow-ttl.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/feeds/routing/batman-adv/patches/999-edgez-halow-ttl.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+--- a/net/batman-adv/main.h
++++ b/net/batman-adv/main.h
+@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
+ #define BATADV_MAX_MTU (ETH_MAX_MTU - batadv_max_header_len())
+ 
+ /* Time To Live of broadcast messages */
+-#define BATADV_TTL 50
++#define BATADV_TTL 8
+ 
+ /* maximum sequence number age of broadcast messages */
+ #define BATADV_BCAST_MAX_AGE 64
-- 
2.50.1
